<title>FRANCE: MOTORCYCLING-LE MANS 24 HOURS RACES LEADING PLACINGS.</title>
<headline>MOTORCYCLING-LE MANS 24 HOURS RACES LEADING PLACINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LE MANS, France 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings in</p>
<p>the Le Mans 24 Hours race, opening stage of the motorcyling</p>
<p>endurance world championship on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Juan Eric Gomez (France)/Doug Polen (U.S.)/Peter Goddard</p>
<p>(Australia), Suzuki 758 laps</p>
<p>2. Jean-Marc Deletang (France)/Jean-Philippe Ruggia</p>
<p>(France)/Christer Lindholm (Sweden), Yamaha 10 laps behind.</p>
<p>3. Eric Mahe (France)/Jean-Louis Battistini (France)/Norihiko</p>
<p>Fujiwara (Japan), Yamaha 18 laps</p>
<p>4. Christophe Guyot (France)/Andre Lussiana (France)/Michel</p>
<p>Simeon (Belgium), Kawasaki 18</p>
<p>5. Philippe Dobe (France)/Christian Haquin (France)</p>
<p>/Jean-Francois Cortinovis (France), Kawasaki 24</p>
<p>6. Therry Paillot (France)/Olivier Ulmann (France)/Vincent</p>
<p>Vivoli (France), Suzuki, 40</p>
<p>7. Philippe Monneret (France)/Emmanuel Maubon (France)/Michel</p>
<p>Amalric (France), Yamaha 41</p>
<p>8. Gilles Ferstler (France)/Bruno Bonhuil (France)/Florian</p>
<p>Ferracci (France), Suzuki 41</p>
<p>9. Jean-Pierre Schneider (France)/Stephane Gabrieli</p>
<p>(France)/Alain Bronec (France), Yamaha 44</p>
<p>10. Eric L'Herbette (France)/Wilfrid Veille (France)/Philippe</p>
<p>Denis (France), Kawasaki 48</p>
<p>Fastest lap: Piergiorgio Bontempi (Italy), Kawasaki 1.45:695</p>
</text>
